==Strategy==
Unsurprisingly, St. Dober is the main threat in this stage. However, this time around the only support he comes with are the various Croakleys that spawn throughout the stage. You can delay fighting them by luring St. Dober close to your base. Use units like [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] to control St. Dober, and damage it with anti-Angel attackers that outrange it. Don't use meatshields or St. Dober will snipe your stack.

Any anti-Angel Ubers or Legend Rares (such as [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]]) will greatly expedite things.

[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]'s knockback against St. Dober is very good here and, with some luck on procs, can even solo the stage.

Once St. Dober is dead, ideally use a fast unit like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to rush into the blind spot of the Croakleys and kill them.

